.TH JOB-INSPECT 1 "2026-03-17" "toolbox" "Toolbox Commands"

.SH NAME
job-inspect \- inspect a toolbox job

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B job-inspect
.IR TARGET

.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B job-inspect
command inspects a toolbox job and prints:

.EX
job directory
status
first 200 lines of log.txt
output files
.EE

The
.I TARGET
argument may be either a job type, such as
.B pdf-ocr
or
.B image-ocr-translate,
or a full job directory path.

When a job type is provided, the most recent matching job under
.B /srv/toolbox/jobs
is selected.

.SH EXAMPLES

Inspect the latest PDF OCR job:

.EX
job-inspect pdf-ocr
.EE

Inspect the latest image OCR translation job:

.EX
job-inspect image-ocr-translate
.EE

Inspect a specific job directory:

.EX
job-inspect /srv/toolbox/jobs/2026-03-17-234942-image-ocr-translate
.EE

.SH FILES

.TP
.B /srv/toolbox/jobs
Directory containing executed toolbox jobs.

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR run-job (1)

.SH AUTHOR
Thiago Ribeiro
